---
// The README's notice, word for word (owner's rule: no piracy tools, the wrapped projects do the core work).
---
<aside class="notice-band" aria-label="Notice">
  <div class="wrap notice-in reveal">
    <span class="mark" aria-hidden="true">!</span>
    <p><strong>Notice:</strong> FramePort doesn't download, share or unlock games. Use games you got legally, for example from
      <a href="https://sidequestvr.com/">SideQuest</a>. FramePort downloads published open-source tools (see
      <a href="#credits">Built on</a>) and adds its own patches so games run on the Frame.</p>
    <p class="poc">FramePort is a proof of concept.</p>
  </div>
</aside>

<style>
  .notice-band { padding-block: 8px clamp(40px, 6vw, 72px); }
  .notice-in { display: flex; gap: 16px; align-items: flex-start; padding: 18px 22px; border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    background: rgba(92, 208, 230, 0.06); border: 1px solid rgba(92, 208, 230, 0.3); }
  .mark { flex: none; width: 28px; height: 28px; border-radius: 50%; display: grid; place-items: center; font: 800 15px/1 var(--font-display);
    color: var(--bg); background: var(--info); }
  .notice-in { flex-wrap: wrap; }
  p { flex: 1 1 calc(100% - 60px); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text); max-width: 100ch; }
  .poc { flex-basis: 100%; padding-left: 44px; font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-2); }
</style>
